# Caddy in front of the costing tool, for a server reached by IP address before it has a
# domain name. Install as /etc/caddy/Caddyfile and set RIC_HOST to the server's address
# (in /etc/default/caddy, or edit the address below).
#
# `tls internal` makes Caddy its own certificate authority. Browsers warn about the
# certificate until Caddy's root is trusted on the machine doing the testing
# (deploy/README.md, "Trusting the test certificate"). The sign-in cookie is marked Secure
# outside Development, so the application cannot be used over plain http:// at all (audit C2).
#
# Caddy redirects http:// to https:// on its own, and passes X-Forwarded-For and
# X-Forwarded-Proto, which the application trusts from 127.0.0.1 only.

https://{$RIC_HOST} {
	tls internal
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
}
